{
  "requirement": "`AgentSettings<D>` identifies the configurations a domain can use in its cache.\nTBV implements this sealed trait for `AgentConfig` and `AgentWithTools<D>`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait AgentSettings<D: Domain>: Settings<D> { }\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover the obligations in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.AgentSettings`.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. `AgentSettings<D>` is the bound that decides which configurations a domain cache accepts.\n2. The trait is implemented for `AgentConfig`.\n3. The trait is implemented for `AgentWithTools<D>`.\n4. The trait is sealed, so third parties cannot implement it. The sealing comes from the `Settings<D>` supertrait.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Sealing:** The `compile_fail` doctest on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#trait[AgentSettings]` tries to implement `AgentSettings<D>` for a third-party struct. It is marked `{test}`. The import paths are valid: `agent` and `domain` are `pub mod` in `lib.rs`, and `AgentSettings` is a `pub trait`. The only plausible reason for the doctest to fail compilation is the missing, inaccessible `sealed::Settings<D>` supertrait.\n- **`AgentConfig` accepted:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted]` passes an `AgentConfig::Bedrock` to `ValidationCache::with_agent`. That function takes `impl AgentSettings<D>`. The test then checks the agent is attached, shared across clones, usable by `refresh_evidence`, and not persisted.\n- **`AgentWithTools<D>` accepted:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[registered_tools_use_the_current_context_and_ordinary_node_ids]` passes `backend.with_tool(...)`, an `AgentWithTools<D>`, to `with_agent`. It asserts that the registered tools reach the agent requests and appear in the tool list, and that a different tool set gives a different list.\n\nBetween them, the tests cover both implementors and the sealing. I found no untested obligation or weak assertion.",
  "references": "cec8dc27c3b2606c94129fd6e5a30835b88f6c749b7486e187768c03410c8bbd",
